IO-19: reject [COVERAGES] percentages outside 0-100 or above 100 in total

handle_coverages() stored a land use's percent without any check. Buildup
and EMC washoff are scaled by it, so 160 % gave 1.6 times the washoff load,
and a negative percent was accepted too. Report ERROR 211 for a percent below
0 or above 100, or one that takes the subcatchment's land uses above 100 % in
total (0.1 % allowed for rounding), with the same rule as the 5.3.0 patch.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-19_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/input/handlers/QualityHandler.cpp b/src/engine/input/handlers/QualityHandler.cpp
index b28c85c..87935bf 100644
--- a/src/engine/input/handlers/QualityHandler.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/input/handlers/QualityHandler.cpp
@@ -265,7 +265,17 @@ void handle_coverages(SimulationContext& ctx, const std::vector<std::string>& li
         const int lu_idx = ctx.landuse_names.find(tok[1]);
         if (lu_idx < 0) continue;
 
-        ctx.subcatches.coverage[sub_idx * n_landuses + lu_idx] = to_double(tok[2]);
+        // A land use covers 0-100 % of the subcatchment, and all of them at
+        // most 100 % (0.1 % is allowed for rounded percentages). Legacy: ERROR 211.
+        const double pct = to_double(tok[2]);
+        double total = pct;
+        for (int m = 0; m < n_landuses; ++m)
+            if (m != lu_idx) total += ctx.subcatches.coverage[sub_idx * n_landuses + m];
+        if (pct < 0.0 || pct > 100.0 || total > 100.1) {
+            ctx.errors.push_back(format_error(ERR_NUMBER, tok[2]));
+            continue;
+        }
+        ctx.subcatches.coverage[sub_idx * n_landuses + lu_idx] = pct;
     }
 }
 
